{"id": 27899, "date": "2015-05-02T11:00:00", "date_gmt": "2015-05-02T18:00:00", "guid": {"rendered": "https://estreetshuffle.com/?p=27899"}, "modified": "2026-07-22T18:38:37", "modified_gmt": "2026-07-23T01:38:37", "slug": "cover-me-rhinestone-cowboy", "status": "publish", "type": "post", "link": "https://estreetshuffle.com/index.php/2015/05/02/cover-me-rhinestone-cowboy/", "title": {"rendered": "Rhinestone Cowboy"}, "content": {"rendered": "<blockquote><p><span style=\"font-size: 13pt;\">\u201cIt was just a song that came up in an instant, you know. A really beautifully written song, and it was always one of my favorites by Glen Campbell.\u201d <em>&#8212; Bruce Springsteen, Variety, October 17, 2019</em></span></p></blockquote>\n<p>Sure, Bruce.</p>\n<p>I&#8217;m sure that&#8217;s all it was: a beautiful song that came to mind in the moment when you were putting together your set list for your <em>Western Stars\u00a0</em>film.</p>\n<p>It probably had nothing to do with its inspiration, a country singer named David Allan Coe, who wore rhinestones and a mask on stage. Why? Because, his father taught him an important lesson:</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px;\"><em>I got the mysterious rhinestone thing from my father. He asked me, \u201dYou know the only way that The Lone Ranger\u00a0can go into town? I said, \u201cNo, I don\u2019t know what you mean.\u201d He said that he has to take his mask off. I thought, what is my dad talking about and trying to tell me? He said, \u201cWell son, you have to wear a mask and then when you don\u2019t want to be David Allan Coe you can take your mask off and go anywhere and not be like\u00a0Elvis with people messin\u2019 with you all the time.</em><sup id=\"cite_ref-Smith_3-1\" class=\"reference\"></sup></p>\n<p><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-attachment-id=\"28079\" data-permalink=\"https://estreetshuffle.com/index.php/2015/05/02/cover-me-rhinestone-cowboy/dac/#main\" data-orig-file=\"https://i0.wp.com/estreetshuffle.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/dac.jpg?fit=1788%2C1842&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"1788,1842\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;Perfection 2400&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;1&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"dac\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://i0.wp.com/estreetshuffle.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/dac.jpg?fit=758%2C781&amp;ssl=1\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-28079 size-full\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/estreetshuffle.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/dac.jpg?resize=758%2C781&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" width=\"758\" height=\"781\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/estreetshuffle.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/dac.jpg?w=1788&amp;ssl=1 1788w, https://i0.wp.com/estreetshuffle.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/dac.jpg?resize=291%2C300&amp;ssl=1 291w, https://i0.wp.com/estreetshuffle.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/dac.jpg?resize=994%2C1024&amp;ssl=1 994w, https://i0.wp.com/estreetshuffle.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/dac.jpg?resize=768%2C791&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/estreetshuffle.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/dac.jpg?resize=1491%2C1536&amp;ssl=1 1491w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 758px) 100vw, 758px\" /></p>\n<p>It&#8217;s probably just happenstance that the song Coe inspired&#8211;made famous by Glenn Campbell (but originally written and recorded by Larry Weiss)&#8211;was about an obscure singer questing for stardom but just barely scraping by, just like Bruce was at the time.</p>\n<div class=\"jetpack-video-wrapper\"><span class=\"embed-youtube\" style=\"text-align:center; display: block;\"><iframe loading=\"lazy\" class=\"youtube-player\" width=\"758\" height=\"427\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/8kAU3B9Pi_U?version=3&#038;rel=1&#038;showsearch=0&#038;showinfo=1&#038;iv_load_policy=1&#038;fs=1&#038;hl=en-US&#038;autohide=2&#038;wmode=transparent\" allowfullscreen=\"true\" style=\"border:0;\" sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-popups allow-presentation allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox\"></iframe></span></div>\n<p>It&#8217;s a <em>complete</em> coincidence that at the very moment Bruce exploded into mainstream stardom with <em>Born to Run</em> in the autumn of 1975, Campbell&#8217;s song was riding the top of the charts.</p>\n<p><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-attachment-id=\"28078\" data-permalink=\"https://estreetshuffle.com/index.php/2015/05/02/cover-me-rhinestone-cowboy/clip_79697004/#main\" data-orig-file=\"https://i0.wp.com/estreetshuffle.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/clip_79697004.jpg?fit=938%2C1805&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"938,1805\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"clip_79697004\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://i0.wp.com/estreetshuffle.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/clip_79697004.jpg?fit=532%2C1024&amp;ssl=1\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-28078 size-full\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/estreetshuffle.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/clip_79697004.jpg?resize=758%2C1459&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" width=\"758\" height=\"1459\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/estreetshuffle.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/clip_79697004.jpg?w=938&amp;ssl=1 938w, https://i0.wp.com/estreetshuffle.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/clip_79697004.jpg?resize=156%2C300&amp;ssl=1 156w, https://i0.wp.com/estreetshuffle.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/clip_79697004.jpg?resize=532%2C1024&amp;ssl=1 532w, https://i0.wp.com/estreetshuffle.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/clip_79697004.jpg?resize=768%2C1478&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/estreetshuffle.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/clip_79697004.jpg?resize=798%2C1536&amp;ssl=1 798w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 758px) 100vw, 758px\" /></p>\n<p>And of course, performing a song named after an imitation wasn&#8217;t at all a wink from a small-town New Jersey rocker to his fans while performing a suite of Western-themed songs from his barn.</p>\n<p>Nope, &#8220;Rhinestone Cowboy&#8221; was just a lovely song to end a film with.</p>\n<p>Sometimes a rhinestone is just&#8230; well, a rhinestone.</p>\n<div class=\"jetpack-video-wrapper\"><span class=\"embed-youtube\" style=\"text-align:center; display: block;\"><iframe loading=\"lazy\" class=\"youtube-player\" width=\"758\" height=\"427\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/NcnM3nju2uQ?version=3&#038;rel=1&#038;showsearch=0&#038;showinfo=1&#038;iv_load_policy=1&#038;fs=1&#038;hl=en-US&#038;autohide=2&#038;wmode=transparent\" allowfullscreen=\"true\" style=\"border:0;\" sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-popups allow-presentation allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox\"></iframe></span></div>\n<p><strong>Rhinestone Cowboy<br />\nReleased:\u00a0</strong><em>Western Stars: Songs From the Film (2019)</em><strong><br />\nFirst performed:</strong>\u00a0April 2019<br />\n<strong>Last performed:</strong> April 2019</p>\n<p>\u00a9 June 17, 2021</p>\n", "protected": false}, "excerpt": {"rendered": "<p>Bruce couldn&#8217;t have chose a more perfect song to end his Western Stars film with than the 1975 classic by a New York songwriter yearning to make it big as a western country star.</p>\n", "protected": false}, "author": 1, "featured_media": 27974, "comment_status": "open", "ping_status": "open", "sticky": false, "template"